    {
      "title": "Canada’s retaliatory US tariffs set to take effect as trade dispute grows",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/07/canada-tariffs-us-trump",
      "description": "<p>Counter-measures covering several sectors come after Trump announced 50% tariffs on Canadian goods </p><p>Canada is set to impose retaliatory tariffs on billions of dollars’ worth of American imports early on Tuesday, escalating a <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/aug/23/canada-us-collapsed-trade-talks-negotiation-breakdown-analysis\">trade fight</a> with its largest trading partner as tensions between US president Donald Trump and Canadian prime minister Mark Carney intensify.</p><p>The tariffs, which take effect at 12.01am on Tuesday, will range from 15% to 50% and apply to products covering C$27.6bn in imports from the US. The measures will target sectors including steel, dairy, appliances, agricultural equipment, pulp and paper, and electronics – industries that have been most affected by US tariffs.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/07/canada-tariffs-us-trump\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-07T23:20:24"
    },
